# Reporting delivery contract

A delivery is the immutable record of exactly what left the repository: a
submitted manuscript, printer PDF, presented deck, or distributed report. The
same lifecycle applies to every reporting type.

## Canonical path

```
reporting/<type>/<artifact>/deliveries/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<milestone>/
├── delivery.yaml
├── payload/                  # exact delivered payload(s)
└── figures/                  # exact figure bytes used, when applicable
```

`<type>` is `papers`, `posters`, `presentations`, or `writeups`. The milestone
is a short stable label such as `submitted-v1`, `printer-final`,
`lab-meeting`, or `funder-report`.

Create it only after explicit human approval:

```bash
python scripts/freeze_delivery.py \
  --type papers \
  --artifact <artifact-slug> \
  --milestone <milestone-slug> \
  --payload <built-file> \
  --figure <figure-file>
```

Repeat `--payload` and `--figure` as needed. `--type` accepts `papers`,
`posters`, `presentations`, or `writeups`; `--execution-id` selects a specific
registered execution and `--date YYYY-MM-DD` selects an explicit delivery date.
Without `--execution-id`, the command reads the current provenance ID, which
must already be registered.

## Required manifest facts

`delivery.yaml` is generated and validated with the delivery. It records:

- artifact type/name, delivery date, and milestone;
- run-time and delivery-time Git revision/dirty-state identity;
- a canonical identity hash plus SHA-256 map for the DVC pointer/lock files;
- registered execution ID and artifact ID;
- the repository source path of each supplied payload and figure; and
- byte size and SHA-256 for every frozen payload and figure.

The execution ID must have exactly one `metadata/runs.csv` row, and the matching
`metadata/provenance/<execution_id>.json` must exist and agree with the IDs.
Missing, duplicate, or ambiguous identity is an error, not a field to guess.

## Immutability and storage

The command stages and installs the delivery atomically, refuses an existing
destination, validates the manifest, and makes the frozen contents read-only.
Do not edit its manifest, payload, or figures afterward. A correction is a new
dated milestone that can point back to the previous one.

Commit text, manifests, and files up to 1 MiB to Git. Put larger binaries under
{{ data_versioning }} at the same logical delivery path and commit the pointer.
The manifest hashes the delivered payload bytes, not merely the pointer.

Legacy `papers/*/submissions/` directories remain valid immutable records after
a template update. Preserve them in place; use `deliveries/` for new freezes.
